  message: "PREMISE RE-CHECKED 2026-09-24 at dev 2c63301739. All five filed rows are still loaded, unchanged:\n- python urllib.request.Request net_send\n- go net/http.NewRequest net_send\n- erlang and elixir ets.new db_write\n- elixir Req.new net_send (io_primitives_overlays/elixir-web-and-db.yaml, loaded by default)\n\nTHE PRE-REGISTERED QUESTION, measured on ONE python fixture (not the cohort A/B this item asks for).\nFixture: key = os.urandom(16) [key_material]; req = Request(url, data=key); urlopen(req).\nClaim: key_material must not reach the network zone. verify-claims --format json.\n- Arm A (current catalogue): violated. Evidence at Request (ddg, confirmed), and at urlopen (ddg_mixed, walk_verdict ESCAPED).\n- Arm B (Request removed from python.yaml:568, in a separate worktree): violated. Evidence at urlopen (ddg, CONFIRMED).\n- Control (urlopen(url, data=key) directly): violated and confirmed in both arms.\nSo on this fixture the flow SURVIVES the deletion, and urlopen's evidence becomes stronger once Request stops being the sink that ends the walk. That points to a free precision fix for the python row. It is not yet shown on a cohort, and go, erlang and elixir were not re-measured.\n\nTWO RECORD FACTS:\n- python.yaml:1729 carries a note on the module urllib.request.Request: \"CONSTRUCTS AND SENDS NOTHING -- already adjudicated by INV-gujoh and WI-gihif\". Meanwhile :568 still rows Request under net_send.\n- WI-gihif (P2, open, filed 08-30) is the same python row. It is not in this item's not_duplicate_of. SURFACED for the owner, not folded.\nFixtures: scratchpad gujoh/, not kept. Recreate them from the three lines above."  # dce7
